      "writtenOn": "2023-06-05T01:40:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Empty proxy is the same as null. I prefer not to suggest passing a proxy with an empty hostin the doc, because I think it\u0027s clearer if there is only one way to do this. It\u0027s also pretty unclear what it might mean to have a valid proxy but an empty host. But it works today so I want to keep it working.\n\nThere is no `proxyInfo.isEmpty()`. Did you mean `proxyInfo.isValid()` ? But that returns true for an empty host.\n\nEven if we added such a method I\u0027m not sure why it\u0027s better to say `proxyInfo.isEmpty()` instead of `proxyInfo \u003d\u003d null`. I think they are identical in all respects except `\u003d\u003d null` is faster. Maybe the one advantage of having `isEmpty` is that then the objects can be non-null and there is less risk of NPE ?",
